NAME
    echoserver - TCP echo server demo

SYNOPSIS
    echoserver [PORT]

DESCRIPTION
    Binds PORT (default 7778), enters listen mode and serves one
    client at a time: every byte received on the connection is sent
    straight back until the peer closes. Exercises the kernel's
    bind/listen/accept server path end-to-end over the real NIC.

    run.sh forwards host loopback port 17778 to the guest's 7778
    (slirp hostfwd), so from the host shell 'nc 127.0.0.1 17778' (or
    bash's /dev/tcp) can drive it; in the guest, run 'echoserver
    7778' in the foreground first. The guest's own 10.0.2.15 is not
    reachable from the host on a plain slirp user network. accept()
    waits at most 20 s; recv()/send() 5 s per call.

EXIT STATUS
    0 after the listener is closed, 1 on socket/bind/listen failure,
    2 on a bad PORT argument.

EXAMPLES
    echoserver
    echoserver 9999

SEE ALSO
    ping(1), tlsdemo, tlsserver, echoserver, man hosts
